// Entry point for the engine's ::bank admin cheat (ClientCheatHandler, staffModLevel >= 3).
//
// The cheat cannot invoke [label,openbank] directly. A script started by the engine with
// ScriptRunner.init(script, player) has an ACTIVE player but not a PROTECTED one, and openbank
// falls through to ~bankpin_start_entry, whose first statement writes %bankpin_flow - a protected
// varp. That failed with:
//     script error: pop_varp %bankpin_flow requires protected access
//       1: [proc,bankpin_start_entry] - bank_pin.rs2:173
//       2: [label,openbank] - bank.rs2:35
// and dropped the connection.
//
// p_finduid(uid) is how every debugproc acquires the protected pointer from a script that was
// handed none, so the cheat comes through here first. This is a LABEL, not a proc, because
// openbank is a label and "Unable to jump to labels from within a proc".
//
// It still goes through openbank rather than ~bankpin_open_bank_real, so a set bank PIN is
// enforced instead of being sidestepped by the cheat.
[label,cheat_openbank]
if (p_finduid(uid) = true) {
    @openbank;
}
